---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import MuteVideo from '@/components/tools/media/MuteVideo.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="mute-video">
  <MuteVideo client:load />
  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to remove the sound from a video</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Drop the video in. MP4, MOV, MKV, WebM and AVI all work.</li>
      <li>If you want, switch on <strong>Also strip metadata</strong> to clear titles, comments, timestamps and GPS tags at the same time.</li>
      <li>Press <strong>Remove audio</strong>. The video stream is copied, not re-encoded, so a large file finishes in seconds.</li>
      <li>Play the result to confirm it is silent, then download it.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Why this is lossless and fast</h2>
    <p>
      A container such as MP4 holds separate video and audio streams. To mute a video, the tool writes
      the container again with only the video stream inside: FFmpeg's <code>-c:v copy -an</code>. No
      frame is decoded, so nothing is re-compressed, and the speed depends on your disk, not your CPU.
    </p>
    <p>
      A video editor usually renders the whole timeline again, which costs time and a generation of
      quality. Here the picture that comes out is byte-for-byte the picture that went in.
    </p>

    <h2>How much space you get back</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Audio in the source</th>
            <th>Saved per minute</th>
            <th>Saved in an hour</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>AAC 128 kbps stereo</td>
            <td>≈ 0.9 MB</td>
            <td>≈ 55 MB</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>AAC 256 kbps stereo</td>
            <td>≈ 1.8 MB</td>
            <td>≈ 110 MB</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>PCM 48 kHz 16-bit stereo</td>
            <td>≈ 11 MB</td>
            <td>≈ 660 MB</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>When you would want a silent video</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Background loops on a website: browsers autoplay only muted video, and an audio track wastes bandwidth.</li>
      <li>Privacy: a clip filmed in an office or hospital may show nothing sensitive, but the conversation in the background can.</li>
      <li>Copyright: remove licensed music before you upload to avoid automated content claims.</li>
      <li>Re-scoring: remove the original sound before you put the clip into an edit with a new soundtrack.</li>
      <li>Smaller files for silent screen recordings that captured unwanted microphone noise.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Keeping the audio instead</h2>
    <p>
      To keep the soundtrack as a separate file, run
      <a href="/extract-audio-from-video">extract audio from video</a> first. In stream-copy mode it
      saves the original AAC or Opus track with no quality loss. To keep the sound but change the
      picture, see <a href="/compress-video">compress video</a> or
      <a href="/resize-video">resize video</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
